diagnostics/class-mutability.em:24:3: `id` is a `const` field of Account, so it cannot change
  a.id = 2
    ^^
Declare it `var id: Int` in Account if it needs to change.
diagnostics/class-mutability.em:25:3: `home` is a `const` field of Account, so it cannot change
  a.home.x = 3
    ^^^^
Declare it `var home: Point` in Account if it needs to change.
diagnostics/class-mutability.em:27:1: `b` is a `const`, so its contents cannot change
  b.count = 1
  ^
Declare `b` with `var` if it needs to change.
diagnostics/class-mutability.em:29:13: Account cannot be a dictionary key
  var keyed: [Account: Int] = []
              ^^^^^^^
A key must be a number, a `Bool`, a `String`, or a tuple or struct made only from valid key types. Lists, other mutable collections, and class objects cannot be keys.
diagnostics/class-mutability.em:30:7: Account and Other cannot be compared
  print(a == Other())
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^
`==` and `!=` compare two values of the same type, and Int and Float compare with each other.
